WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.220
A drop of pond water can hold living things from all three domains.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.580
A domain is the largest group in classification.

3
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.300
You may see algae, an amoeba, and tiny animals.

4
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:16.980
Other specks are too small to make out.

5
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.480
How could you sort living things you have never seen before?

6
00:00:21.533 --> 00:00:23.733
The first question is about the nucleus.

7
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:28.253
A nucleus is a compartment wrapped in membrane that holds the DNA.

8
00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:31.213
A eukaryote has cells with a nucleus.

9
00:00:32.073 --> 00:00:35.473
A prokaryote is an organism whose cells have no nucleus.

10
00:00:36.473 --> 00:00:38.393
Bacteria and Archaea are prokaryotes.

11
00:00:39.393 --> 00:00:40.633
Eukarya are the eukaryotes.

12
00:00:41.567 --> 00:00:45.007
Bacteria and archaea look alike under a light microscope.

13
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:47.287
So we need other evidence.

14
00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:53.087
One kind is ribosomal RNA, a molecule every cell uses to build proteins.

15
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:55.847
Its sequence differs between the two.

16
00:00:56.747 --> 00:00:57.887
Another is the cell wall.

17
00:00:58.807 --> 00:01:01.507
Most bacteria have peptidoglycan in the wall.

18
00:01:02.627 --> 00:01:03.627
Archaea walls have none.

19
00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:07.247
Only sequence or chemical evidence can tell them apart.

20
00:01:07.247 --> 00:01:08.247
Bacteria and archaea look alike under a light microscope.

21
00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:09.950
Now take a cell with a nucleus.

22
00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.130
Eukarya have four kingdoms.

23
00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.030
A kingdom is the rank just below domain.

24
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.050
Plants have many cells and cellulose walls.

25
00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.730
Most plants are autotrophs, which make their own food.

26
00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:23.770
Fungi have chitin walls.

27
00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.150
They absorb their food, and many are decomposers.

28
00:01:28.150 --> 00:01:30.010
Animals have many cells and no walls.

29
00:01:30.870 --> 00:01:33.430
They are ingesters, which take food inside the body.

30
00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:39.290
Any other eukaryote, single celled or a many celled alga such as kelp, is a protist.

31
00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:42.433
These questions make a dichotomous key.

32
00:01:43.313 --> 00:01:47.033
A dichotomous key is a set of paired choices that leads you to a group.

33
00:01:47.913 --> 00:01:51.193
A key works only for the organisms and traits built into it.

34
00:01:51.973 --> 00:01:54.013
A species also gets a two part name.

35
00:01:54.833 --> 00:01:57.133
The genus comes first, with a capital letter.

36
00:01:57.913 --> 00:02:00.593
The specific epithet comes second, in lower case.

37
00:02:01.533 --> 00:02:03.233
Together the two words name the species.

38
00:02:04.053 --> 00:02:05.893
The blue crab is Callinectes sapidus.

39
00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:10.677
So how can we classify an organism we have never seen before?

40
00:02:11.657 --> 00:02:13.117
Ask the trait questions in order.

41
00:02:13.937 --> 00:02:17.237
Where looks are not enough, check the sequence or chemical evidence.

42
00:02:18.177 --> 00:02:22.637
The three domains are branches of one tree, worked out from sequence comparisons.

43
00:02:23.737 --> 00:02:25.597
Branches show relatedness, not rank.

44
00:02:26.377 --> 00:02:27.497
The drawing is simplified.

45
00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:32.397
Archaea and Eukarya are more closely related to each other than to Bacteria.
